ral health services under Medicare.</p><p>Specifically, the bill increases payments for integrated behavioral health services that are provided by physicians under Medicare for 2027-2029, with payments increased by 175% in 2027, 150% in 2028, and 125% in 2029.</p><p>The bill provides funds for FY2025-FY2029 for the Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services to contract with entities to provide technical assistance to primary care practices that want to adopt models for behavioral health integration.</p>","updateDate":"2026-03-18T17:08:58Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"COMPLETE Care Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:40:49Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:40:49Z"}
